# The image carries the repo as-is (see Dockerfile), so this file is the only
# thing keeping "as-is" from meaning "including a git history, a browser and
# every screenshot ever committed".
#
# node_modules matters most: `npm ci --omit=dev` installs the runtime deps in
# the layer above, and copying a local tree over the top would replace a clean
# production install with whatever a dev machine happened to have — including
# playwright, which is larger than everything else here put together.
#
# Note what is deliberately NOT here: package.json and package-lock.json. The
# static nginx image this replaced excluded both, because it never installed
# anything. This one runs `npm ci`, and a .dockerignore that hides the manifest
# from the COPY that feeds it fails the build on the first layer.
.git
.github
node_modules
npm-debug.log
.dockerignore

# Dev-only tooling and output. None of it is reachable from index.html, and
# screenshots/ alone is larger than everything being served.
tests
tools
screenshots
*.md
